tms6747  TI's rts6740 matches a thrown pointer to a class against a handler for a pointer to one of its public bases and hands it over UNADJUSTED: cl6x 7.4.4's own build of this program prints 'B* 1 0' on TI's C6747 simulator (measured 2026-10-05, C1b), and cpp11's build - whose _ZTI1D is word for word cl6x's - prints the same. VM6747 does what rts6740 does, so the case cannot hold clang's answer here; tools/c6747/release-check holds TI's measured answer for it instead (docs/CONFORMANCE.md).
